Handle MPZ zero before deriving an end pointer.

mpz_init_zero represents zero with len=0 and dig=NULL. mpz_as_int_checked nevertheless formed
dig + len before checking whether there were any digits. That is undefined pointer arithmetic in
C, and Capstone correctly faults when the resulting cincoffset uses a non-capability NULL base.

Return the representable zero value before forming the digit end pointer. A focused EXTRA+MPZ run
changes int_big_mod.py, int_big_pow.py and int_big_zeroone.py from capability faults to PASS; all
eleven adjacent tests retain their PASS status and result words.

diff --git i/py/mpz.c w/py/mpz.c
index e9fd0f45f..59834f1ab 100644
--- i/py/mpz.c
+++ w/py/mpz.c
@@ -1561,3 +1561,7 @@ bool mpz_as_int_checked(const mpz_t *i, mp_int_t *value) {
 bool mpz_as_int_checked(const mpz_t *i, mp_int_t *value) {
     mp_uint_t val = 0;
+    if (i->len == 0) {
+        *value = 0;
+        return true;
+    }
     mpz_dig_t *d = i->dig + i->len;
